## Context
Source: Fable (claude-fable-5-1) and Astra (gpt-6-astra) review of the ruleset, 2026-11-01; reports in the session scratchpad, findings verified against main by the session. Astra finding, verifiable.

`rules/prose-adherence-tests.md:18` puts standing editorial decisions in
`docs/editorial-brief.md`. `rules/zotero.md:25` makes `docs/` git-ignored in
full (`*.md` included). The brief is therefore never committed, durable
decisions live in one checkout only, and `skills/gaze/references/prose-panel.md`
skips the editorial-brief auditor silently when the file is absent (a fresh
clone or a reviewer worktree).

## Decision for the author
Where the brief lives: a tracked path (e.g. `editorial-brief.md` at the repo
root, or `docs/` re-included for that one file), then the rule, the panel and
the `paths:` trigger move together.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The brief has a tracked home; prose-adherence-tests.md, prose-panel.md and the paths: glob name it
- [ ] Existing briefs in paper repos are located and moved (ticket there, per cross-project rule)
